Note that Program 07 is a comprehensive audit verification test exercising every working subsystem in Eathon.

To compute linearTransform taking x as integer, weight as integer, bias as integer returning integer,
  Let weighted be x times weight.
  Return weighted plus bias.
End function.

Display text of Eathon Audit Verification Suite Starting end text.

Note that 1 verifies arithmetic precedence and negative unary operators.
Let alpha be integer 50.
Let beta be integer 12.
Let gamma be alpha plus beta times 4 minus neg 10.
Display gamma.

Note that 2 verifies conditionals and relational comparisons.
If gamma is equal to 108 then,
  Display text of Precedence Check Passed end text.
Otherwise,
  Display text of Precedence Check Failed end text.
End if.

Note that 3 verifies While and Repeat loops.
Let sumLoop be integer 0.
Let idx be integer 1.
While idx is at most 6 repeat,
  Set sumLoop to sumLoop plus idx.
  Set idx to idx plus 1.
End while.

Repeat 4 times,
  Set sumLoop to sumLoop plus 100.
End repeat.
Display sumLoop.

Note that 4 verifies function call with 3 parameters.
Call linearTransform with 15, 3, 25 into transformed.
Display transformed.

Note that 5 verifies bitwise operations, arrays, raw memory offsets, and structures.
Let bitVal be 9 shifted left by 3 bitwise or 5.
Display bitVal.

Allocate array table of 4 integers.
Store 31415 into element 3 of table.
Load element 3 of table into arrOut.
Display arrOut.

Allocate memory block of 32 bytes.
Write 65535 at address block offset 16.
Read integer from address block offset 16 into memOut.
Display memOut.

Define structure Vector2D with fields vx as integer, vy as integer.
Create vec as Vector2D.
Set field vx of vec to 300.
Set field vy of vec to 400.
Get field vx of vec into vxVal.
Get field vy of vec into vyVal.
Let manhattan be vxVal plus vyVal.
Display manhattan.

Note that 6 verifies 2D Tensor matrix multiplication, ReLU clamping, and reduction sum.
Create tensor matA with dimensions 2, 2.
Set cell 0, 0 of matA to 4.
Set cell 0, 1 of matA to neg 3.
Set cell 1, 0 of matA to 2.
Set cell 1, 1 of matA to 5.

Create tensor matB with dimensions 2, 2.
Set cell 0, 0 of matB to 1.
Set cell 0, 1 of matB to 2.
Set cell 1, 0 of matB to 3.
Set cell 1, 1 of matB to 4.

Create tensor matC with dimensions 2, 2.
Multiply tensor matA by tensor matB into matC.
Activate relu on tensor matC.
Sum tensor matC into tensorTotal.
Display tensorTotal.

Note that 7 verifies key value table operations.
Open database kvStore.
Insert key 7 with value 8888 into kvStore.
Query key 7 from kvStore into kvOut.
Display kvOut.

Display text of Eathon Audit Verification Suite Complete end text.
